hat we're  seeing now is the Fed you know fed share  power we're looking investors saying hey  you're moving too quick we are trying to  tighten Financial conditions make things  more difficult and really keep things  tight so that the real economy kind of  starts to slow down and those job  increases start to slow down one thing I  thought was very interesting about the  press conference from Fed chair Powell  is he talked a lot about individuals you  know we talked a lot about the jobs  Market he talked a lot about what  individuals have in their savings really  didn't spend much time at all talking  about corporations about how  corporations are flush with cash right  now so they can afford to have a couple  not so great quarters and still keep  prices High  he didn't talk about net profit margins  for corporations which are record highs  and are expected to move higher through  this year and those net profit margins  mean how much corporations are making  after they pay for higher prices so even  though the things they're buying are  getting more expensive they're raising  their prices at an even faster Pace  didn't talk anything about that or the  effect that these price raises are  having and as you know I talked about  this in a video that we did I want to  say it was back in June of this year why  corporations love inflation corporations  love inflation because it gives them  cover to raise prices and they raise  those prices by more than inflation and  that actually makes inflation keep going  higher Fed chair Jerome Powell didn't  talk about that at all I think that's a  very important thing we have to keep our  eye on last thing I want to mention  before we get out of here I know I'm  running long so I appreciate everyone  that stuck with me that's still here  with us on Market takes I want to talk  about how Fed chair Jerome Powell ended  his press conference uh today and it was  interesting because he was asked the  question about recession and about the  the odds for a soft Landing he said  quote the inflation picture has become  more and more challenging you talk about  how some of these supply chain issues  have resolved and you would have  expected Goods inflation to come down  now but that really hasn't uh what he  said was with regard to the inflation  picture becoming more and more  challenging that means we have to have  policy become more restrictive and that  narrows the path for a soft Landing  Powell really saying you know what we  might have to have a recession it might  be bad folks might be suffering hurting  we're okay with that because we've got  to get recession and control that looks  like the big picture here and that's  probably why you're seeing a lot of the  action that you are in markets look I am  Dion Robert Bowen reporter for the Wall  Street Journal this has been Market  takes like I said I know you could have  been anywhere in the world but you were  here with me and I appreciate that thank  you that's going to do it for us here on  Market takes we will see you next time  please come back and join us
 

